{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fb6ad280346362a580dd3b1ba5464da5eea3146f40ecf0a8f3a682476d6fa006", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d81f4e123247c0fd5b17e7c5bef790c3dd27a7eafea54c8bb7f24e3baf21a77a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe notion of smoothness for groupoids in functors on <MATH_0001> is\ndefined as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:751cfcc7df618344bf5b0169c8c72cf059dcf688230502e6ec344281948131c6", "unit_id": "tag:06KH:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$s, t: R \\to U$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-smooth-groupoid-in-functors}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f7968e37ec624d70d98856276ecb33c445c340753d3fffefd4eddbe76f5049b4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:759ca0bb18fb295a4da38964ccf7151aae95db7b5abcc8702e44f4f4f9447366", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a groupoid in functors on <MATH_0002>. We\nsay <MATH_0003> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>smooth<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0004> are smooth.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9c5f6e0d30f2c3ae9c4c26b30c771b13c0fbda2b9200f8511b41aa016a6bfc64", "unit_id": "tag:06KI:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0002": "$[U/R]$", "MATH_0003": "$(U, R, s, t, c)$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to [U/R]$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-cofibered-groupoid-projection-smooth}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-quotient-morphism}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-smooth-groupoid-in-functors-warning}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a0530e081ced6b838c80b595a72f9672ba888c0c7f4061d3661a1fdfb761019e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8d126ff8fe047e7ae1d1f0d8437670f60572ff3441236badcea4deae3cda6a84", "source_text": "We note that this terminology is potentially confusing:\nif <MATH_0001> is a smooth groupoid in functors, then the quotient\n<MATH_0002> need not be a smooth category cofibred in groupoids as defined in\nDefinition <REF_0001>.\nHowever smoothness of <MATH_0003> does imply (in fact is equivalent to)\nsmoothness of the quotient morphism <MATH_0004> as we shall\nsee in\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:61d164eb455be54a77ec205a9a2f09c6127214bc44c97b45a0bb1c94171add67", "unit_id": "tag:06KJ:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\underline{R_0}, \\underline{R_1}, s, t, c)|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\underline{R_0}, \\underline{R_1}, s, t, c)|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0004": "$R_1$", "MATH_0005": "$R_0$", "MATH_0006": "$s$", "MATH_0007": "$t$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-smooth-morphism-power-series}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-smooth-power-series-prorepresentable-smooth-groupoid-in-functors}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bad781cd984c94344efa09b47a8ef028915e0b05e03883142ee7e7fa048a2191", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:19576d7177d6f9f816755640a49076b50b48f305d3a82cb943bb04501dd1cc1d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe a prorepresentable groupoid in functors on <MATH_0002>.\nThen <MATH_0003>\nis smooth if and only if <MATH_0004> is a power series over <MATH_0005> via both <MATH_0006>\nand <MATH_0007>. This follows from\nLemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:430413f73c848364764d74fa0456de88359f493985ef363580081637dfd299bd", "unit_id": "tag:06KK:statement"}
